              "text": "The Scholar’s Guide to Arithmetic",
              "marks": [
                "italic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " by Bonnycastle, 1795 is one of the most popular arithmetic books ever written. It contains this exercise: ‘If a cardinal can pray a soul out of purgatory, by himself, in an hour, a bishop in three hours, a priest in five and a friar in seven, how long would it take them to pray out three souls from purgatory, all praying together?’",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
