            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In 105 hours they can pray out 176 souls together; scale this time to three souls.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Use a common time of $105$ hours. The cardinal, bishop, priest and friar can pray out $105$, $35$, $21$ and $15$ souls respectively.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Souls in 105 hours} &= 105+35+21+15\\\\\\text{Souls in 105 hours} &= 176\\end{align*}$$\n\nTogether, one soul takes $\\frac{105}{176}$ hours.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Time for three souls} &= 3\\times\\frac{105}{176}\\\\\\text{Time for three souls} &= \\frac{315}{176}\\text{ hours}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
